WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.100
What is a click worth? The auction and the numbers.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.150
This is the video for module 1 of Paid Advertising with Google Ads.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:15.600
Most adverts interrupt people. A search ad shows only after someone has typed what they want into Google.

4
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:25.510
When a person in Ibadan types inverter installation near me, she is telling you her need, her place and often her hurry. That is called search intent.

5
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:33.030
Every search runs a fresh auction among advertisers whose keywords match. Nobody books a fixed spot.

6
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:40.700
The winner is not simply the person who bids most. Quality counts too, and quality is something you control.

7
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:51.320
The most common mistake in Google Ads is setting a budget and bids without knowing what a customer is worth. This video shows you how to work it out.

8
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:59.370
Google gives each keyword a Quality Score from 1 to 10. Think of it as a warning light. It has three parts.

9
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:05.190
First, expected click-through rate, or CTR: how likely your ad is to be clicked.

10
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:12.130
Second, ad relevance. If this is low, the keyword probably sits in the wrong ad group.

11
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:20.380
Third, landing page experience. If this is below average, cleverer ads will not fix it. Fix the page.

12
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:33.850
In the course example, Installer A bids 300 naira with good quality, takes the top spot and pays about 251 naira a click, while Installer B bids 500 naira and sits lower.

13
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.300
Here is the chain you will use in every proposal. Start with the average sale value.

14
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:48.080
Next, gross profit per sale: the sale value times the gross margin, after materials and labour.

15
00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.620
Then the close rate. Out of every 10 leads, how many pay?

16
00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:58.010
Multiply gross profit by the close rate, and you have the lead value.

17
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:04.930
Decide what share of lead value the business will spend on ads. That is the target cost per lead.

18
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:17.170
Multiply that by the landing page conversion rate, the share of clicks that become leads. That is your maximum CPC, the most you can pay for a click and still make money.

19
00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:27.040
Here is Tunde, who installs home solar systems in Ibadan. These figures are illustrative, so always use your client's own numbers.

20
00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:38.780
His average job is about 1,200,000 naira. His margin is 25%, so gross profit per job is 300,000 naira.

21
00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:48.970
From his records, 1 in 10 enquiries becomes a paid job. That is a 10% close rate, so each lead is worth 30,000 naira.

22
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:56.090
He is willing to spend one third of that on ads, so his target cost per lead is 10,000 naira.

23
00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:05.320
His service page turns about 5% of visitors into enquiries. So his maximum CPC is 500 naira.

24
00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.590
If Keyword Planner shows most of his keywords well below that, the market is workable.

25
00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:20.250
Keyword Planner is a free tool inside Google Ads. Set the location to the area the business serves, and look at the bid ranges.

26
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:28.790
If the high-range bids sit below your maximum CPC, go ahead. Start with buying words like price, near me or install.

27
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:40.690
If bids are well above your maximum CPC, you will lose money on most clicks. Improve the conversion rate or close rate first, or target narrower, cheaper terms.

28
00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:55.930
This is your client's money, so protect it. Divide the monthly budget by 30.4 to get the daily budget. For Tunde, 300,000 naira a month becomes about 9,900 naira a day.

29
00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:04.470
A busy day can spend up to 2 times that, but the month stays capped. Tell the client before launch, so a busy day does not cause panic.

30
00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.750
And recheck bid ranges before every proposal.

31
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:16.210
To remember. Search ads reach people who already said what they want, and good quality can win a better spot for less.

32
00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:24.220
Lead value is gross profit times close rate. Maximum CPC is target cost per lead times conversion rate.

33
00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.430
When the numbers are tight, raise the conversion rate or close rate.

34
00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:38.960
Now try it on a real business. Ask the owner for sale value, margin and close rate, then work out lead value and maximum CPC.

35
00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:46.800
Record 10 keywords from Keyword Planner and mark each one green, amber or red. Continue with the lessons below.
